  "title": "Square Field Parameterizations",
  "category": "hydraulic_properties",
  "deck": "Synthetic conductivity and storage examples comparing structured and triangular supports, inline units, and vertical profiles.",
  "summary": "This case builds one compact two-zone square domain and maps the same conductivity field onto structured and triangular meshes. It also illustrates how inline units and depth-profile modes are normalized before the solver stage.",
  "case_setup": [
    "Unit-square domain split by one diagonal into granite and micaschist zones.",
    "Structured and triangular meshes generated from the same target cell count.",
    "Depth dependence illustrated with `none`, `exponential`, and `tabulated` profiles."
  ],
